  "caption": "Quinn bought Nordic walking poles very enthusiastically — and ended up with poles flailing and dragging behind.\n\nKay explains that Nordic walking poles add upper-body work and more cardio effort without extra joint load — but they don't really take much load off the knees.\n\nWhat can help: plant the pole near your back foot, angled back, and push past your hip; set the length to about two-thirds of your height, with the elbow near a right angle; use the strap or glove so your hand can relax; add separate balance training. A short lesson can help.\n\nGet checked for chest pain or breathlessness, calf pain that comes with walking and eases with rest, new falls, or night joint pain.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
